From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Utkarsh Dalal <dalal.utkarsh@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:04:29 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Windows: make volatile code regions opt-in

DetectVolatileRegion was on unless FEX_EXP_VOLATILE=0. On JIT runtimes it
misfires: TMNT: Shredder's Revenge (FNA/.NET) spends most of its main thread
recompiling, runs about 10x slower and never creates a D3D device. Enable it
only for FEX_EXP_VOLATILE=1; titles that need it (Age of Empires IV) set it.
---
 Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp b/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp
index 304f29e8e..26e56352e 100644
--- a/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp
+++ b/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp
@@ -258,7 +258,7 @@ bool InvalidationTracker::HandleRWXAccessViolation(FEXCore::Core::InternalThread
 void InvalidationTracker::DetectVolatileRegion(uint64_t FaultAddress) {
   static const bool Enabled = [] {
     const char* Value = getenv("FEX_EXP_VOLATILE");
-    return !Value || Value[0] != '0';
+    return Value && Value[0] == '1';
   }();
   if (!Enabled) {
     return;
